  "architecture": "agentic",
  "question": "What does LoRA freeze, and roughly what fraction of a model's parameters does it actually train?",
  "answer": "LoRA leaves the entire pretrained model **frozen** \u2013 none of the original weight matrices are updated.\u202fInstead, it only learns the small, low\u2011rank adapter matrices that are injected alongside each frozen weight matrix.\u202fBecause those adapters are tiny, LoRA trains only a **very small fraction of the total parameters \u2013 typically well under\u202f1\u202f% of the base model\u2019s parameters**\u3010lora-and-parameter-efficient-fine-tuning::0\u3011\u3010lora-and-parameter-efficient-fine-tuning::1\u3011.",
